rity in last month's election  besting incumbent tulepa saleli  malalagawi  matafa was once his deputy pm until she  broke away to challenge him there have  been weeks of turmoil in the south  pacific nation  the supreme court had to intervene and  ordered parliament to convene  so the new government could take power  still ahead their sense of smell is  helping sniff out covid19  some optimism to share tonight in terms  of how fast and how accurately covet 19  can be detected  researchers in the united kingdom  working with specially trained dogs  found the animals quickly identified the  virus 94  of the time now this is important  because there are parts of the world  still battling rising infections and as  crystal gamansing reports  these canines may be our new friends in  this pandemic fight  that's a good boy those puppy dog eyes  may make you melt but their noses could  actually save your life the dogs could  detect correctly if somebody was  infected with covet  94 of the time and what's really  incredible about these dogs  is that they can do it really really  quickly the findings come from a joint  research project between london school  of hygiene  and tropical medicine and durham  university  for months they have worked with six  medical detection dogs  teaching them to recognize the scent of  covet 19  and testing the dog's ability to  identify samples  and interestingly they could do it  irrespective of the level of virus that  the patients had  so they could detect people with low  viral loads  just as readily as they could those  people with high  viral loads the findings have not been  peer reviewed but they  are in line with other canine trials a  pilot project at the helsinki airport  last year  saw dogs correctly identify nearly every  sample  thai researchers reported their dogs had  a 95 percent success rate  with roughly 2 000 samples dogs are now  being deployed in bangkok  the extra help comes as the virus takes  a heavy toll more cases have been  reported so far this year  than in the whole of 2020.  on current trends the number of deaths  will overtake  last year's total within the next three  weeks  quickly identifying cases and isolating  those who are ill  is key to keeping the virus from  spreading this is something that could  really change  the way in which diagnostics look  because you could  do a rapid screen and then follow it up  with a pcr test  researchers say it's still early but  several countries are working with dogs  to confirm how our four-legged friends  can help in the fight against coveted  19.  crystal gomencing global news london  up next the new feature in dating apps  that may  improve your shot at love  a couple in india skirted that country's  coveted 19 restrictions and  tied the knot on a chartered flight  crammed with family and friends  there were 160 people on board the  two-hour flight  india's aviation authority has now  launched an investigation  the airline spicejet says the plane was  booked by a travel agent  airport staff say they were unaware of  the couple was planning the sky high  ceremony  are you looking for love dating isn't  easy in a pandemic  first there's the risk of getting the  virus in an intimate moment  then there's the vaccination situation  now some apps have an added feature to  give single people  another shot at finding a perfect match  here's catherine ward  the pandemic has dealt a tough hand for  those looking for love  you don't really get a feel of exactly  how the person is when you're just  chatting with them online  while i have been out of the dating game  for some time  my friends tell me the stakes feel so  much higher with covet 19.  i found that i was always the person  having to create the boundaries around  physical distancing  and to state my boundaries and those  things and some guys were into it and  some guys weren't  pre-pandemic people might have been  searching for a partner of a certain age  gender religion or background but in  2021  many want to know your vaccine status  people do want to know and people are  asking up front  even if being vaccinated isn't like 100  your thing  or important to you your health should  be in the u.s on friday the government  teamed up with several dating websites  trying to encourage people to get a shot  social distancing and dating  were always a bit of a challenging  combination on okcupid for example  users in the us can now display badges  indicating they've been vaccinated and  also filter out people who haven't  if a person participates the company  also provides incentives they plan to  expand this globally  it's not clear if other companies will  follow suit  in a statement from bumble a  spokesperson says vaccine badges and  complementary super swipes are currently  u.s only it's a kind of vaccine passport  in some ways  still some experts are not discounting  the idea proof of vaccination opens  doors to all kinds of things  like maybe theaters travel schools  certain jobs  why not dating because while a vaccine  may or may not  be a deal breaker i did meet someone  online i knew that he  was eligible for a vaccine and he just  hadn't signed up yet it very well  could be part of your love story it's  kind of a condition of dating me  that you make an appointment to get  vaccinated and he said okay i will  catherine ward global news toronto it's  a whole new level  to modern love and that is global  national for this monday night i'm robin  gill  tonight your canada is the prairie lily  riverboat in saskatoon  we would love to see your corner of the  country so please keep sending your  photos to viewers at globalnational.com  thank you for watching donna friesen  we'll be back tomorrow and i'll see you  next weekend  have a great night  you
 

